# CODEOWNERS — enforced on `tylluan-montaraz` (community branch) via branch
# protection's "require code owner reviews". A community PR touching any of
# these paths cannot merge without a review from the team account, regardless
# of how many other approvals it has.
#
# Rationale (2026-07-26): this repo now accepts external community
# contributions via fork+PR into `tylluan-montaraz`. CI workflows and
# security-critical code are the two places a malicious or careless PR could
# do real damage (secret exfiltration via a modified workflow, an ACL/gate
# bypass in security code) — see docs/reference/security/github_agent_incidents.md
# for the documented 2025-2026 incidents this defends against
# (tj-actions/changed-files, pull_request_nightmare, CamoLeak, GitLost).
#
# Everything NOT listed here can be approved by any reviewer with write access.

# CI/CD — the single highest-risk surface for a public repo taking PRs.
# A workflow change is how a fork PR would try to exfiltrate secrets or
# escalate to RCE on a runner (see pull_request_nightmare, tj-actions).
/.github/workflows/          @Forja-orca
/.github/CODEOWNERS          @Forja-orca

# Security-critical kernel code — ACL, sandbox, coherence gate, signal loop,
# agent contracts. A subtle change here is the hardest kind of bug to catch
# in review if it isn't required review.
/crates/tylluan-kernel/src/security/  @Forja-orca
/crates/tylluan-kernel/src/transport/http/auth.rs  @Forja-orca

# Repo-level config that affects every build/release.
/Cargo.toml                  @Forja-orca
/deny.toml                   @Forja-orca
/.tylluan/                   @Forja-orca
